fact, formulas of the $h^*$-polynomial and the normalized volume of $\\nabla^{\\rm PQ}_G$ of a join graph $G$ are presented.\n\n## PQ-type adjacency polytopes of join graphs\n\nHidefumi Ohsugi, Akiyoshi Tsuchiya\n\nPublished: 2021-03-28\n\nComments: 18 pages, 1 figure\n\nNote:\n\nJournal: Discrete and Computational Geometry 70 (2023), 214--235\n\nDOI: 10.1007/s00454-022-00447-z\n\ncomplete multipartite graph graph lattice polytope polytope polynomial lattice\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nPQ-type adjacency polytopes $\\nabla^{\\rm PQ}_G$ are lattice polytopes arising from finite graphs $G$. There is a connection between $\\nabla^{\\rm PQ}_G$ and the engineering problem known as power-flow study, which models the balance of electric power on a network of power generation. In particular, the normalized volume of $\\nabla^{\\rm PQ}_G$ plays a central role. In the present paper, we focus the case where $G$ is a join graph. In fact, formulas of the $h^*$-polynomial and the normalized volume of $\\nabla^{\\rm PQ}_G$ of a join graph $G$ are presented. Moreover, we give explicit formulas of the $h^*$-polynomial and the normalized volume of $\\nabla^{\\rm PQ}_G$ when $G$ is a complete multipartite graph or a wheel graph.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKreweras words and the Cyclic Sieving Phenomenon (https://mathematik.univie.ac.at/eventsnews/nachrichtenvolldarstellung/news/kreweras-words-and-the-cyclic-sieving-phenomenon/?cHash=eddcc6e381cd4916ed14c2eb123b6cb0&no_cache=1)\nciteturn8search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; AG Diskrete Mathematik | 27.01.2026 15:00 - 16:30\n\nMona Gatzweiler (University of Vienna) ... In this talk, I want to discuss a conjecture by Hopkins and Rubey from 2022 on Kreweras words fulfilling cyclic sieving and the ongoing work (joint with Christian Krattenthaler) on this conjecture.\n\n# \n\n# Kreweras words and the Cyclic Sieving Phenomenon\n\nAG Diskrete Mathematik | 27.01.2026 15:00 - 16:30\n\nMona Gatzweiler (University of Vienna)\n\nABSTRACT:\nThe cyclic sieving phenomenon is a beautiful interplay of combinatorics and algebra, satisfied by permutations, tableaux, non-crossing matchings,… and an ever growing list of objects.  In this talk, I want to discuss a conjecture by Hopkins and Rubey from 2022 on Kreweras words fulfilling cyclic sieving and the ongoing work (joint with Christian Krattenthaler) on this conjecture.\n\nOrganiser:\n\nI. Fischer, M. Schlosser\n\nLocation:\n\n#### BZ 9, 9. OG, OMP1\n\n##  Verwandte Links\n\n  * https://www.dmg.tuwien.ac.at/nfn/agdm.html\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPQ-Type Adjacency Polytopes of Join Graphs | Article Information | J-GLOBAL (https://jglobal.jst.go.jp/en/detail?JGLOBAL_ID=202302236811489620)\nciteturn8search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; # PQ-Type Adjacency Polytopes of Join Graphs ... Ohsugi Hidefumi ... Tsuchiya Akiyoshi ... Basics of graph theory\n\nArt\n\nJ-GLOBAL ID：202302236811489620   Reference number：23A1704395\n\n# PQ-Type Adjacency Polytopes of Join Graphs\n\nジョイングラフのPQ型隣接ポリトープ〖JST・京大機械翻訳〗\n\n  * Publisher site Copy service {{ this.onShowCLink(\"http://jdream3.com/copy/?sid=JGLOBAL&noSystem=1&documentNoArray=23A1704395&COPY=1\") }}\n  * Access JDreamⅢ for advanced search and analysis. {{ this.onShowJLink(\"http://jdream3.com/lp/jglobal/index.html?docNo=23A1704395&from=J-GLOBAL&jstjournalNo=W2035A\") }}\n\nAuthor (2)：\n\nOhsugi Hidefumi\n\nAbout Ohsugi Hidefumi\n\n(Department of Mathematical Sciences, School of Science, Kwansei Gakuin University, Sanda, Hyogo, Japan)\n\nAbout Department of Mathematical Sciences, School of Science, Kwansei Gakuin University, Sanda, Hyogo, Japan\n\n  * Search \"201551000096692265\"\n  * Search \"Department of Mathematical Sciences, School of Science, Kwansei Gakuin University, Sanda, Hyogo, Japan\"\n  * Detailed information\n\n, \n\nTsuchiya Akiyoshi\n\